{"abstract":[{"text":"Change which Markdown syntax a parser understands by choosing its block parsers and inline transformers.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConfiguringTheParser"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Configuring the Parser"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Markdown dialect supported by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is defined by two parameters:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"block parsers","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", each represented as a subclass of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/BlockParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which recognize the block structure of a document, and","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"inline transformers","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", each represented as a subclass of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/InlineTransformer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which recognize markup within the text of a block.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The initializer of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" accepts both components optionally. The default configuration (neither block parsers nor inline transformers are provided for the initializer) is able to handle Markdown based on the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://commonmark.org","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let parser = MarkdownParser(blockParsers: MarkdownParser.headingParsers + [","                              FencedCodeBlockParser.self,","                              BlockquoteParser.self,","                              ListItemParser.self","                            ])"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The order of the block parsers and of the inline transformers matters. The block parsers are tried in order on each line, the first one that recognizes the line starts a block, and a line that none of them recognizes belongs to a paragraph. A configuration without ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/IndentedCodeBlockParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", as above, therefore treats indented text as a paragraph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Use-the-predefined-parser","level":3,"text":"Use the predefined parser","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" objects are stateless (beyond the configuration of block parsers and inline transformers), there is a predefined default ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" object accessible via the static property ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser/standard","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendedMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" have their own shared instances, too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Derive-a-parser-with-a-different-configuration","level":3,"text":"Derive a parser with a different configuration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"New Markdown parsers with different configurations can also be created by subclassing ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and by overriding the class properties ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser/defaultBlockParsers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser/defaultInlineTransformers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Here is an example of how class ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendedMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is derived from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by overriding ","type":"text"},{"code":"defaultBlockParsers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", by specializing ","type":"text"},{"code":"standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a covariant fashion, and by overriding the factory method ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser/documentParser(blockParsers:input:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which is needed for supporting definition lists.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["open class ExtendedMarkdownParser: MarkdownParser {","  override open class var defaultBlockParsers: [BlockParser.Type] {","    return self.blockParsers","  }","  private static let blockParsers: [BlockParser.Type] = MarkdownParser.headingParsers + [","    IndentedCodeBlockParser.self,","    FencedCodeBlockParser.self,","    HtmlBlockParser.self,","    LinkRefDefinitionParser.self,","    BlockquoteParser.self,","    ExtendedListItemParser.self,","    TableParser.self","  ]","  override open class var standard: ExtendedMarkdownParser {","    return self.singleton","  }","  private static let singleton: ExtendedMarkdownParser = ExtendedMarkdownParser()","  open override func documentParser(blockParsers: [BlockParser.Type],","                                    input: String) -> DocumentParser {","    return ExtendedDocumentParser(blockParsers: blockParsers, input: input)","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A subclass that adds state has to take care of its thread safety. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/BlockParser":{"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"BlockParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parses one particular type of Markdown blocks. Class ","type":"text"},{"code":"BlockParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" defines","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a framework for such block parsers. Every different block type comes with its own subclass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"BlockParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifie